<title>SINGAPORE: Takeover talk pushes Parkway shares up.</title>
<headline>Takeover talk pushes Parkway shares up.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Takeover rumours pushed property and healthcare group Parkway Holdings Ltd's shares up on Thursday morning, dealers said.</p>
<p>But by 0220 GMT, Parkway shares retreated to Singapore $4.46 after rising to a high of S$4.68 on 1.4 million shares in the early minutes of trading.  </p>
<p>Dealers said Malaysia's Berjaya Group could be accumulating shares for a possible takeover.</p>
<p>They attributed Berjaya's interest to a synergy of its pharmaceutical interests, namely through its associate Pantai Hospital Bhd.</p>
<p>Parkway Holdings owns Gleneagles International Pte Ltd which runs the Gleneagles chain of hospitals.</p>
<p>Parkway officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>--SIngapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
